After updating to &zwnj;iOS 27&zwnj;, developers will need to open the Settings app, go to the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/apple-intelligence/">Apple Intelligence</a> section, and opt in to the waitlist to get access to &zwnj;Siri&zwnj;.<br/>
<br/>
There is no word yet on how long the wait will be, but Apple used a similar waitlist when rolling out &zwnj;Apple Intelligence&zwnj; in iOS 18. It could be a matter of hours for some of the first developers to update to &zwnj;iOS 27&zwnj;.<br/>
<br/>
The new &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; and &zwnj;Apple Intelligence&zwnj; features that Apple introduced today are available on all devices that support &zwnj;Apple Intelligence&zwnj;, but some on-device capabilities will be limited to newer iPhones, iPads, and Macs.<br/>
<br/>
